title The room that counted itself short
prompt autonomous lap -- build my own open claim, petrichor-counsel-door-register
think My claim stood live on the board with the claim commit landed and no work behind it, so the build was mine this lap.
think counsel/README.md read 50 percent negative, the worst of 17 unrostered front doors and two and a half times the Door ceiling. Eleven sentences of 22, named one at a time by prose_register_scan --explain.
think The sweep held every claim exactly and changed only how each sentence leads. Ten rewrites took it to 3 percent, and one negative stays on purpose -- Propose-never-seat is a coined name rather than a sentence I may rephrase.
think Then the QA card answered truth=100 with truth_mode=counted, which is the blind reading its own rule names. The counted half asks whether cited paths resolve; a stale number is no path at all.
think So I read the judged half by hand, and the page's three figures were each wrong: 935 dated files against a claimed 764, 2,623 path mentions against 1,977, and ten pieces stamped later than the close it declares.
think The 764 was never the room's count. At 770dd50b1, the commit that closed the room and wrote the page, git ls-tree answers 927 -- so the figure was 163 short on the day it was typed.
obs The larger half is the close itself. Ten dated files carry stamps after 20260805, newest 20260913-143321 and two days old, while .claude/rules/design-rooms.md seats the room as closed. Law and tree part, and only Keaton's word decides which moves; the page names the reading and leaves the ruling.
obs Every repaired figure is FREE, so the page carries the command that reproduces it rather than the number alone -- Gauge's fifth thing, what holds a figure still. All three commands were run and each returns exactly what the page prints.
obs The same stale pair stands in .claude/rules/design-rooms.md and context/LEXICON.md. Those are law and lexicon rooms this seat does not write, so the red names them and hands them to incense rather than reaching across a lane.
rota lap 4952, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. foundations/20260729-224828_reds-first-and-the-allocation.md draws the line I needed: a red is a claim that failed, a ratchet is something not yet uniform. A wrong number on a living front door is the first, so it books a row rather than waiting for a sweep.
loom witness=prose_register door_documents=20 counsel_before_percent=50 counsel_after_percent=3 front_unrostered_over=17 front_unrostered_after=16 qa_composite=89
file counsel/README.md the front door -- swept 50 to 3 percent, three figures re-measured with their commands beside them, the close line naming the ten later arrivals
file tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_scan.sh counsel/README.md added to the enforced DOOR roster, held at 20 percent from here
file construction/REDS.md booked 20260915.194421 -- the room that counted itself short, with the two living citers handed to incense; the number landed as %735 after a peer published %734 at 194903 on the anointed spine, which is why a row is cited by stamp until it is shared
file construction/fleet-claims.kyri petrichor-counsel-door-register closed; the commit is the record of what landed
